## Done this session

**1. Ghost-writer root cause PROVEN and FIXED** (build `06E672C2`, deployed + verified). O_DIRECT dumps showed 11 live old-generation mounts heartbeating into a re-mkfs'd LUN plus 1,972 stale lock records — the cause of the sess130 zero_silent_loss shutdown. Fix: (a) **self-fence** — heartbeat thread re-checks the super's fs_uuid every 2s and force-shuts-down if the device was reformatted under it (`P131-SELF-FENCE`); (b) fs_gen tag in heartbeat records with foreign-gen filtering in monitor/claim/stale-mask/MDS-resolve; (c) foreign-volume lock slots recyclable in `find_slot_skip`. Verified by deliberate repro: re-mkfs under two live mounts → both fenced in ~1-2s, LUN stayed clean, new generation mounted clean, fenced nodes unmount clean.

**2. zero_silent_loss blocker re-isolated as pure throughput.** Correctness now passes (silent=0). Criterion times out (300s RULE-0 budget): the 16-node same-dir mkdir storm runs ~10-16 creates/s, needs ≥64/s. P106 timeline analysis (clocks verified synced ~10ms): 131 EX grants / 269 releases for 80 creates, p50 tenure 100ms — **each ~100-170ms EX tenure accomplishes <1 create**; the cost is inside the tenure (create + release drain pipeline), not the handoff gap (p50 5.6ms) — plus a starvation tail at full size.

**3. Built decomposition probes** (build `6FDA6A850CC4D9009F3F642`, compiled clean, NOT yet deployed): `P106-EXREL` now reports `drain_ms` (bast_process entry → pre-publish) and `tail_ms` (publish → unlock); new always-on `P131-WAITLONG` logs any lock grant that waited >1s with resource detail.

